{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group","id":944851,"title":"CtL2E criticisms from my group","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-06T08:08:39-07:00","id":944851,"title":"CtL2E criticisms from my group","content":"First of all, I'm in love with the Chronicles/2E rules for the most part. Mortal CoD, Werewolf 2E, and the brand-new Promethean 2E are all freaking amazing. That said, switching over to the partially-revealed 2E CtL rules really hurt my 18-month chronicle. I've been meaning to write up my group's criticisms since the game ended in June.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Things both my players and I disliked about the new rules:</u></b><ul><li>The ability for changelings to escape any situation is questionable. One major plot in our game surrounded a civil war in the freehold, and the inability to question or provide due-process to defeated enemies limited the game significantly. There's suddenly no point in inter-Court conflict, as the only options for enforcement are now genocide and shutting the hell up. (I know you couldn't imprison changelings before, but you could at least hold them long enough for a quick trial.) There's no way to provide fae justice, whether in your chronicle you conceive that as an honorable pursuit or a mere mockery of law and order.</li> <li>The changes to Pledges reduce the meta-drive to roleplay interactions with humans. Whereas in 1E my players would actively try to learn more about NPCs so that they might form Pledges with them, in 2E they rarely cared to roleplay interactions with mortals.</li> </ul><u><b>Things I disliked as Storyteller:</b></u><ul><li>I personally dislike the shift in theme towards &quot;Wyrd as legend made manifest&quot; and away from &quot;Wyrd as the power of promises.&quot; I'm not a fan of fairies in general, but CtL 1E really captured me with the idea of a bunch of paranoid Rumpelstiltskins trading promises more valuable than all the gold in the world. The authors moving away from that idea tells me that I'm not the target demographic of 2E. Which is fine and all, but I obviously don't like it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> <li>Dual Kith is way too good NOT to take from a meta perspective, yet it dilutes the &quot;feel&quot; of a character. A Brewer/Woodwalker Elemental--a goblinfruit alchemy specialist--doesn't have the same flair as either a Brewer Elemental or a Woodwalker Elemental: it gets a little muddled when you combine the kiths. I don't mind OP abilities, but I want OP abilities to ADD to the game's panache, not dilute it. (Good examples of OP merits include &quot;Professional Training&quot; and WtF2E's &quot;Embodiment of the Firstborn&quot;. They <i>enhance</i> a character concept rather than muddle it.)</li> </ul><u><b>Things we actually liked a lot:</b></u><ul><li>Huntsmen. Very cool. We couldn't wait to find out what Arcadian Weapons were, so we made up a system rather like Storied Weapons from one of the Armory books, but included that they did strange damage in order to &quot;preserve&quot; a Changeling. For example, they might reap Clarity instead of Health or Glamour. I introduced the Nemean Lion as a huntsman, complete with his pelt as his Arcadian Weapon.</li> <li>The new Contracts. They're both more powerful and Experiences-efficient, although minor balance tweaks should be made.</li> <li>The new Clarity system, including Seeming blessings and curses. We loved that it could fluctuate wildly, and I found that I had more players volunteering breaking points in exchange for beats and the Acuity condition. (The &quot;volunteer your own breaking points&quot; method is my personal preference as ST and as a player, and GMC/2E has really improved our group's roleplay thanks to its breaking-points-for-experience mechanic.)</li> <li>The suggestion that unique Courts be designed for each chronicle. While I don't love <i>everything</i> about the new Court system, I do like being told to make s*** up instead of follow exact formulae.</li> </ul>In summary: for me, the worst part was the shift in themes. Pledges (and by extension, the metaphysical nature of Contracts) taking the backseat really killed the fun for me as ST, and I burned out very quickly. For my players, the inability to interrogate or try any offending changeling ruined any subplots involving changeling nemeses, and since there aren't any &quot;equal footing&quot; fae nemeses, that was a majority of the conflict. Did we still have fun doing random fairy stuff, like throwing parties for Sin-Eaters and therapeutically helping people rediscover their faith? Sure, of course. But the driving soul of the game felt lost after the change to 2E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8335-pondrthis","name":"pondrthis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T08:51:52-07:00","id":944874,"title":"","content":"I think one thing worth keeping in mind is that only the smallest fraction of the book's fluff is available via the spoilers, so your misgivings may be based on misunderstandings or content which was overhauled between the drafts we saw and the final product, so I wouldn't write off the writing of 2e as a thematic shift away from what you like just yet. It's very possible the wording and language of it will be clarified before the final product drops and you'll find it more to your taste.<br /> <br /> The dual-kith being too good thing might be an issue solved by restricting some merits or abilities to being mono-kith maybe? So like, that merit which lets you enhance your effect Wyrd score for the effects your kith grands might require you to be a single-kith. Little stuff like that might help make it a more attractive option I your game.<br /> <br /> I know in my vampire games, I originally thought the same about Bloodlines, but more recently my players and I found ourselves just preferring to play the regular Clans because they're very elemental in a way that's satisfying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T09:05:19-07:00","id":944882,"title":"","content":"To be clear, my problem with Dual Kith isn't its &quot;OPness&quot;, but rather the fact that it's so attractive from a meta perspective <i>while simultaneously being unattractive from a world-building perspective.</i><br /> <br /> I embrace OPness. If I didn't, there's no way I'd love WtF2E, haha. I just think something that EVERY PLAYER WILL PICK should have some soul to it; as it stands, we'll have Sandwalker/Manikin combos that make no sense (I use these two randomly, of course) just to get both mechanical bonuses. Unlike additional Tells for Wolf-Blooded, combining two Kiths is often just weird from a thematic perspective. All Tells are &quot;werewolf-like&quot;, but most Kiths are very unique and, to an extent, mutually exclusive.<br /> --------------------<br /> With regards to the &quot;don't judge till it's done&quot; argument, you're right, of course. I feel like the entire version is taking a thematic shift because: 1) Pledges (oaths) are now easy to escape in most cases, 2) Goblin Vows replaced Pledges from a mechanical standpoint, and they're greatly diminished in scope, and 3) the Courts and Huntsmen, two HUGE components of the universe, are both highly entrenched in the &quot;Story&quot; rather than true names, pledges, and fae law.<br /> <br /> Edit to clarify: The Courts are now of more ritual than political/&quot;legal&quot; importance, which is meh to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8335,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8335-pondrthis","user":"pondrthis","date":". 08-06-2016, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8335-pondrthis","name":"pondrthis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T09:59:41-07:00","id":944918,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind that Changeling tricks won't work on cold iron. You can still hold them with a properly constructed prison, or find a way to reduce their glamour to zero (thorns from the hedge should do), both of which were good practices even before 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T12:10:34-07:00","id":944990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pondrthis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=944882#post944882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be clear, my problem with Dual Kith isn't its &amp;quot;OPness&amp;quot;, but rather the fact that it's so attractive from a meta perspective <i>while simultaneously being unattractive from a world-building perspective.</i><br /> <br /> I embrace OPness. If I didn't, there's no way I'd love WtF2E, haha. I just think something that EVERY PLAYER WILL PICK should have some soul to it; as it stands, we'll have Sandwalker/Manikin combos that make no sense (I use these two randomly, of course) just to get both mechanical bonuses. Unlike additional Tells for Wolf-Blooded, combining two Kiths is often just weird from a thematic perspective. All Tells are &amp;quot;werewolf-like&amp;quot;, but most Kiths are very unique and, to an extent, mutually exclusive.<br /> --------------------</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall reading in the Kith devblog that it's explicitly possible to refluff a Kith to be more to your tastes, like taking the one about fire, inspiration and candles and giving it an aesthetic of lightning, which can make it fit more with the other kith that you combine it with. I don't know if that will totally solve your feelings of discomfort but it might help with aesthetic clashing if that's the chief both. I would work with your players to encourage them to pick combinations that make logical or thematic sense (sometimes True Fae are weird, so it might not make sense in our world but it should probably have internal consistency with whatever went down in Arcadia.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pondrthis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=944882#post944882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With regards to the &amp;quot;don't judge till it's done&amp;quot; argument, you're right, of course. I feel like the entire version is taking a thematic shift because: 1) Pledges (oaths) are now easy to escape in most cases, 2) Goblin Vows replaced Pledges from a mechanical standpoint, and they're greatly diminished in scope, and 3) the Courts and Huntsmen, two HUGE components of the universe, are both highly entrenched in the &amp;quot;Story&amp;quot; rather than true names, pledges, and fae law.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind, I'm trying to help think through this instead of offering definitive answer, but the impression I got is that Fae Law and the like IS Story. Promises are narratively the framework of Courts, Huntsmen and the powers that Changelings have. <br /> <br /> Maybe in the Hedge, which I believe is the first sourcebook we might see some things expanded upon in how they work or how they may develop beyond starting characters to greater power?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pondrthis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=944882#post944882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit to clarify: The Courts are now of more ritual than political/&amp;quot;legal&amp;quot; importance, which is meh to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like, particularly in the context of fairies but also in general that &quot;ritual&quot; and &quot;political&quot; are actually extremely hard to separate. Courts form as much out of a need for order and stability among Changelongs as they do to act as a ritual bulwark, and someone's interest or investment in the Court could very possibly be more political in nature. I just don't see how ritual precludes politics? I think I might not be understanding properly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T12:17:07-07:00","id":944996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pondrthis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=944882#post944882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be clear, my problem with Dual Kith isn't its &quot;OPness&quot;, but rather the fact that it's so attractive from a meta perspective <i>while simultaneously being unattractive from a world-building perspective.</i><br /> <br /> I embrace OPness. If I didn't, there's no way I'd love WtF2E, haha. I just think something that EVERY PLAYER WILL PICK should have some soul to it; as it stands, we'll have Sandwalker/Manikin combos that make no sense (I use these two randomly, of course) just to get both mechanical bonuses. Unlike additional Tells for Wolf-Blooded, combining two Kiths is often just weird from a thematic perspective. All Tells are &quot;werewolf-like&quot;, but most Kiths are very unique and, to an extent, mutually exclusive.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my experience, fae are as varied as you can imagine, and probably beyond (but since this is a tabletop game let's just settle with what we can imagine). I adhere to the idea that any two kiths could be combined into any Dual Kith you can think of - your noted one here, Sandwalker/Manikin, could have been a statue made of scarabs, able to recombine and be reshaped at their maker's will, or perhaps they were a snowman, or, to be more literal, they could have been a sand soldier who stood guard and one day decided to venture to a new post. While I agree there's not a lot of reason for players not to take Dual Kith mechanically, and that the aforementioned Changeling concepts could just as easily be one kith if not the other, it is ultimately up to the player to take it or not and to be creative with the resulting Changeling.<br /> <br /> Even if you were to go with something like, say, Nix/Ifrit, where one manipulates water and another fire, or even a Nix/Fireheart where they control water yet can spark fire with their fingertips, there's a fairly easy way to go about that: make them into a being who boiled water. They could have been a human bunsen burner, a tea kettle, a bath tender or even have had the role of making geisers work in their gentry's realm. They'd need to generate heat to do so, so naturally above water they'd cause fire with such heat, and they'd need to manipulate the water to make sure it all stayed in the same place so it could be boiled.<br /> <br /> In my eyes, no kith is mutually exclusive. Yes, the pairings can be odd, but they have an amount of sense to them from the context of the world they escaped. If you can't make sense of them, modify them to be more thematically linked as the notes suggest. If you have a Snowskin/Ifrit but you want them to control snow instead of fire so they'd be a proper snow queen, change the Pyrokinesis effect to Cryokinesis. If you have a space themed Changeling, Airtouched could be renamed Gravity Born or somesuch.<br /> <br /> Of course, if you don't like it, well, it's not my place to tell you that you should. I personally love the freedom this gives, but I can appreciate that not everyone will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T16:25:39-07:00","id":945135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=944990#post944990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like, particularly in the context of fairies but also in general that &quot;ritual&quot; and &quot;political&quot; are actually extremely hard to separate. Courts form as much out of a need for order and stability among Changelongs as they do to act as a ritual bulwark, and someone's interest or investment in the Court could very possibly be more political in nature. I just don't see how ritual precludes politics? I think I might not be understanding properly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't speak for the context of fairies, as I'm more into the fairy <i>tale</i> (as in, morality play) aspect than tales of fairies themselves. But to me, politics for the sake of increasing one's own power and inevitably diminishing the powers of others--as humans and True Fae are both wont to do--is radically different from the act of mutual preservation inherent to the 2E bulwark system. YMMV, of course, but my interpretation of Courts in 1E relied more on the idea of Changelings as social and emotional parasites. The 2E system seems to imply that fairies look after their own, which is fine and fae-like in a sense, but not in the spirit of CtL 1E; in 1E, fae created the Courts as a way to enforce honor on their neighbors out of paranoia. What with the rules regarding escape from bonds and oaths, Courts can't even really enforce that anymore--the Bulwark is the new &quot;purpose&quot; for Changelings to come together.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my eyes, no kith is mutually exclusive. Yes, the pairings can be odd, but they have an amount of sense to them from the context of the world they escaped. If you can't make sense of them, modify them to be more thematically linked as the notes suggest.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that a lot, if not most, pairings can be made to &quot;make sense&quot;. I think the only dual NPC I made was a mosquito-man Nix/(some insect kith). Our PCs <i>mostly</i> made sense, like a Gargantuan/Hunterheart pairing. I think the issue I have is that, if they expect every troupe to be rigging together a little of this and a little of that, the presentation shouldn't include dozens of Kiths and the merit Dual Kith. They should just say, &quot;get together with your storyteller to make your Kith and Kith Blessing; here are a handful of examples.&quot; There's no point of such a comprehensive list and merit if 1) everyone will take the merit and 2) everyone will thus have to effectively design their own Kith.<br /> <br /> As I said in my OP, I <i>like</i> to be told to make s*** up. It's the core of roleplaying and storytelling. But presenting an apparently-comprehensive framework that hides the fact that I'd be better off making s*** up is disingenuous from a communication perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8335-pondrthis","name":"pondrthis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T16:38:43-07:00","id":945146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pondrthis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=945135#post945135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't speak for the context of fairies, as I'm more into the fairy <i>tale</i> (as in, morality play) aspect than tales of fairies themselves. But to me, politics for the sake of increasing one's own power and inevitably diminishing the powers of others--as humans and True Fae are both wont to do--is radically different from the act of mutual preservation inherent to the 2E bulwark system.</div> </div> </div> </div>In what way does the presence of the bulwark system preclude the former from happening? In a system where Changelings actually can sell one another out for another shot at escaping the Huntsman, is a bulwark system which helps mitigate the Huntsmen (notably, not neutralize them) solely an act of mutual preservation, or is it a matter of coming together collectively to protect each other AND to watch one another to ensure that a society of mutual cooperation does not collapse under the tangible and real ability to betray one another for the sake of freedom?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pondrthis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=945135#post945135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">YMMV, of course, but my interpretation of Courts in 1E relied more on the idea of Changelings as social and emotional parasites. The 2E system seems to imply that fairies look after their own, which is fine and fae-like in a sense, but not in the spirit of CtL 1E; in 1E, fae created the Courts as a way to enforce honor on their neighbors out of paranoia. What with the rules regarding escape from bonds and oaths, Courts can't even really enforce that anymore--the Bulwark is the new &quot;purpose&quot; for Changelings to come together.</div> </div> </div> </div>They socially parasitise one another through the Courts in a way not dissimilar to how people do. As to the idea that it implies that Changelings look out for one another, I again feel it prudent to mention that, in what we have had made available to us, they point out the constant possibility of taking a token from a Huntsmen to sell out another Changeling.<br /> <br /> I think the fact that the limited wordcount we've seen does not belabor the inability of the Changelings to trust one another is more a consequence of seeing limited words, and even then, I think when you're showcasing material for people to actually use, it's more conducive to play to talk about how said systems work than spending more words on how they fail. I trust the corebook will do the work of showing us how they fail, and given the explicit existence and temptation of the tokens the Huntsmen give, I suspect that's just one of the most obvious failure points.<br /> <br /> They gather in Courts to protect themselves from the True Fae and to protect themselves from each other. Changelings are no less paranoid, is it any wonder that motleys are important?<br /> <br /> That's just my perspective, I wouldn't jump to conclusions yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T18:46:46-07:00","id":945212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=945146#post945146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In what way does the presence of the bulwark system preclude the former from happening?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't. I don't mean to imply that it does; sorry if I miscommunicated. The <i>focus</i> has shifted in the provided draft, which is both undeniable and precisely what I don't like. I have been clear that this is the opinion of my troupe, and not objective truth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=945146#post945146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to the idea that it implies that Changelings look out for one another, I again feel it prudent to mention that, in what we have had made available to us, they point out the constant possibility of taking a token from a Huntsmen to sell out another Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, of course. A key point to note, in my mind, is that dealing with Huntsmen seems to be an unacceptable-yet-inevitable behavior. This contrasts, in my mind, the 1E fact that changelings are mostly toxic to each other, and the closer you are to another changeling, the more negative/abusive your relationship is likely to become. Does that mean there won't be some flavor in 2E showcasing fae toxicity? No, of course not. But again, we see the focus shifting--that fact was <i>everywhere</i> in 1E's text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=945146#post945146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">limited wordcount</div> </div> </div> </div>This is all we can comment on. It's just as disingenuous to say that I can't extrapolate the leaked text as it would be for me to say that you must accept my commentary as representative of the finished product.<br /> <br /> You make a good point when you say that hints are best focused on how the setting <i>works. </i>I would argue that situations in which the setting <i>works</i> should be the BEST insight into the average changeling's mind, though, rather than cherry-picked exceptions.<br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Your excellent post got me thinking, and it provided me with another minor complaint. If the Tokens of Reprieve are supposed to be the main way Changelings can betray one another now that Oaths are easily escaped, that's a problem in my mind. In 1E, someone could be an oathbreaker without committing the cardinal sin, which is imprisonment or aiding in the imprisonment of another changeling. It seems that now there are no shades of gray between &quot;total douchebag&quot; and &quot;godless loyalist puppet&quot;.<br /> <br /> Oathbreaking was something that, at least in my troupe's chronicle, generally resulted in a trial and, often, exile. Conspiring with the Gentry was a kill-on-sight thing; discovering someone has earned a Token of Reprieve would fall more in this category, I think. (That said, I appreciate that the text explicitly noted that most changelings understand what drives another to earn a Token, and see it as an obvious temptation.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8335-pondrthis","name":"pondrthis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T22:54:49-07:00","id":945963,"title":"","content":"I would be interested in reading about more people opinions concerning what they liked and did not like while play testing the material already released. Would anyone else like to share?<br /> <br /> I would like to note Tokens of Reprieve are objects easily taken from vanquished Privateers, thus ownership of one is not condemning evidence of cooperation with a Huntsman. At least that's what my Darking would say when you found a Token of Repreive in his effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 08-08-2016, 01:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T15:21:30-07:00","id":947256,"title":"","content":"There is alot of strong competition amoung Changeling feats, Mantle which is hugely powerful, Goblin Vows, Hollow, Court Goodwill, Tokens, Fae Mount, Hedge Spun Tokens, Hedge Beast Companion (HBC alone is far more powerful the Dual Kith by itself, even at 1 dot), and that's just the merits we've seen.<br /> <br /> So there is no must have merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T20:17:03-07:00","id":947447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pondrthis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group#post944851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, I'm in love with the Chronicles/2E rules for the most part. Mortal CoD, Werewolf 2E, and the brand-new Promethean 2E are all freaking amazing. That said, switching over to the partially-revealed 2E CtL rules really hurt my 18-month chronicle. I've been meaning to write up my group's criticisms since the game ended in June.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Things both my players and I disliked about the new rules:</u></b>[LIST][*]The ability for changelings to escape any situation is questionable. One major plot in our game surrounded a civil war in the freehold, and the inability to question or provide due-process to defeated enemies limited the game significantly. There's suddenly no point in inter-Court conflict, as the only options for enforcement are now genocide and shutting the hell up. (I know you couldn't imprison changelings before, but you could at least hold them long enough for a quick trial.) There's no way to provide fae justice, whether in your chronicle you conceive that as an honorable pursuit or a mere mockery of law and order.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this about Caging a Dream? No hand cuffs or sealed room can stop you? If you can find a seal-able portal you can jump into the hedge. That caging a dream, right?<br /> <br /> Well some really easy ways my brothers and I have found(played around with) around this power is(unconsciousness is not a prison, its a state of being by the way).<ul><li>We found a windowless room in a basement. We took the door off the room so you couldn't seal it(the requirement for a portal is that you can seal the portal. Can't close the door, can't open a portal). We chained a mean dog to the door. Yes you can leave at any time. No there is nothing stopping you. Are you a combat spec? Add more dogs, poisons, a bare trap or two. Cut the lights and maybe add a little tid bit about a bomb trap(real or not people tend to not want to be blown up). This is all in a basement, all your doing is wasting time till you get to someone who can handle you.</li> <li>A lord dug a pit. He put a fence around said pit. He had lots of hedge beasts around said fence. Yes you can climb out of the pit at any time; even a child could do it, but mind the hungry monsters.</li> <li>we found a topless water tank, a big one, about the size of a kiddy pool but 10 feet tall around the edges. We put a guy with a bit of wood at the top of it. You get out and you get the shaft.</li> <li>Knock them out. Put someone in handcuffs. Hang them by said cuffs over the side of a cliff. Have a guy with a gun at the ready. Why yes they can slip out of the cuffs, thank you for asking.</li> <li>douse them in oil and light a ring of fire around them. If they might be immune to that live wire fences and other barriers work, again as long as they can't open or close it.</li> </ul><br /> No personal restraints and lock boxes. <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Those are the rules for holding a changeling. </span></span></span>Pretty much changeling jailors don't buy hindges or hand cuffs. Make them not want to get out, and keep them from the hedge unless what is in the hedge is worse. The simple empty doorway with a couple of guards next to it can trap most changelings. I like the &quot;we bought a crane just to hang people by the belt over a 2000 foot drop. We're also a marksman's club. So escape. Please.&quot; Option, but that is just me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11660-sleepychicken","name":"SleepyChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11660_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T09:20:20-07:00","id":949351,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't put it past a few courts to cut off a person's foot with an axe or simply shoot them in both knees either. Just because they can't be trapped doesn't mean you have to let them run away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T17:27:02-07:00","id":949652,"title":"","content":"I've had thoughts on using frailties to keep a Changeling captive. Had a little daydream imagining the potential Special Containment Procedures Ziggy would have if the SCP got a hold of him. 1) Whenever he gets too close to the walls, a computer would challenge him to a game, which he would be compelled to play. 2) I have a bit of an oddball bane in mind for Ziggy: Faraday cages. Instead of the standard aggravated damage, being in a Faraday cage immobilizes him and combines two breaking point triggers: Being restrained as a Beast, and his fear of immobilization.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, make the door, restraints, or whatever out of it, or possibly even just decorated with a bane. Result: They have to spend willpower to act against their bane in addition to glamour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T00:51:19-07:00","id":953709,"title":"","content":"I think this is overly focused on jailing changelings. In my mind, a freehold's justice system would be a lot more informal and rely more on social pressures than locks and chains. Unless your suspect is a wandering murderhobo, the way you keep them in town is to tell them the whole freehold is watching them. A sort of house arrest would work, too. &quot;Swear to me that you won't leave your apartment before all this is cleared up, or there will be trouble.&quot; The sealing or oath would double as an alarm if they try and run. This all feels a thousand times more likely than maiming them or holding them at gunpoint for days. Some of you are suggesting, like, super-unnecessary Bond villain contraptions.<br /> <br /> <br /> As to the subject of imprisonment as punishment, I expect that to also be very, very rare. Changelings would be more likely to exile someone from the community or put them under a punishing oath, I think.<br /> <br /> For your freehold civil war, it may help to look at Toronto writeup. A traitorous court tried to stage a coup. The perpetrators are not put on trial. The leaders are executed and the rest are told &quot;Swear loyalty to one of the other Courts or die.&quot; That's what your civil warring Courts would likely be doing. &quot;Swear loyalty to us (or at least to stop fighting) or be executed/exiled/hit with a very large stick.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":478,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","user":"Intrepid Vector","date":". 08-19-2016, 04:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T01:22:46-07:00","id":953714,"title":"","content":"If a Freehold needs to bind a Changeling, and for some reason extracting a sworn Pledge not to leave isn't good enough, why aren't cold iron chains solving the issue?<br /> <br /> The Caging a Dream rules are really only an issue with mortal imprisonment (i.e. police unknowingly trying arrest a Changeling) or dealing with supernaturals who don't understand Changelings. Freeholds shouldn't have any substantial problem with it, and 99 times out of 100 can work off of Pledges rather than needing break out the iron.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T14:15:02-07:00","id":954608,"title":"","content":"Would an old well not work? A pit 6 to 8 feet in diameter and at least a 100 feet deep seems pretty difficult to climb out of without rope or gear for most. I think a room could be constructed with an open doorway that is designed to hold metal bars at 6 inch intervals that after placed could be locked into place with the locks out of reach. All that if you don't want to simply have guards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T10:00:09-07:00","id":956389,"title":"","content":"Cold iron prisons and restraints were definitely a possibility here and any large court with a decent power base could and would obtain such. Changeling criminals are just as unlikely as any to not care about the social ramifications of their actions. So I doubt most would concede to a hardcore Pledge without severe plot convience. I assume we are talking political dissidents peddling alternative courts and violent offenders against the freehold are our culprits here. If such fae cared about their motley and families nor w then their cause I think they wouldn't have acted out to begin with.<br /> <br /> It may be exhausting to hammer a couple expensive chunks of raw iron into a holding cell. But it can be done and there is great reason to do so. Especially when the convict is losing their sanity. That's the last thing a Monarch wants escaping into the thier Hedge backyard.<br /> <br /> Cold Iron stops and is inert to Wyrd Magic. Smart Courts employ it ruthlessly and just deal with the expense. Especially Monarchs uninterested in losing power.<br /> <br /> And finally all this leads to power and it's corruptive influence. Most fae would say an Iron prison is unjust. But so is murdering a rival out of anger or jealousy. And mundane prisons and mundane justice is ineffective against the fae. Life isn't fair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4036-khalvin8","name":"Khalvin8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4036_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T11:51:21-07:00","id":959357,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to withhold judgment until the complete book comes out. That said, I do have several misgivings. For me the first edition of Changeling the Lost was about as perfect a game as WOD (or COD now, I suppose) could have made, with a myriad of ways for a clever player to exemplify the theme of beautiful madness and build the character they truly wanted to play. So it is with a heavy sense of foreboding and consternation that I'm watching all of these major changes to the rules taking place. Whereas 2nd Werewolf and Vampire can be said to mostly be the same game with minor updates and adjustments to properly fit in with 2nd edition and the introduction of a new antagonist to shake things up a little, Changeling sounds more and more foreign to me. I don't want to give up on the game, but I'm definitely prepared to just stick with 1st edition entirely if the new edition can't live up to the old setting. But like I said, I'm not going to make that call until I have the final version of the rules in my hands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T10:20:06-07:00","id":962354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=959357#post959357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to withhold judgment until the complete book comes out. That said, I do have several misgivings. For me the first edition of Changeling the Lost was about as perfect a game as WOD (or COD now, I suppose) could have made, with a myriad of ways for a clever player to exemplify the theme of beautiful madness and build the character they truly wanted to play. So it is with a heavy sense of foreboding and consternation that I'm watching all of these major changes to the rules taking place. Whereas 2nd Werewolf and Vampire can be said to mostly be the same game with minor updates and adjustments to properly fit in with 2nd edition and the introduction of a new antagonist to shake things up a little, Changeling sounds more and more foreign to me. I don't want to give up on the game, but I'm definitely prepared to just stick with 1st edition entirely if the new edition can't live up to the old setting. But like I said, I'm not going to make that call until I have the final version of the rules in my hands.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know man, Werewolf had some significant changes both to mechanics and to the setting. The Gifts system was completely restructured, Rites got their own completely new system, Harmony was re-built from the ground up to focus on balancing between extremes, Kuruth got significantly expanded upon and the system for determining Kuruth triggers was changed as well, Lunacy was divorced from Willpower and tied into the Breaking Point system and split into three different Conditions (four with the right Gift Facet), the Tribes were changed from roles in werewolf society to organizations founded on common sacred prey, Unahir were excised from the game... The fact that it still feels quintessentially <i>Werewolf the Forsaken</i>, that anyone could look at the two editions side by side and say they were &quot;mostly the same game with minor updates and adjustments&quot; is a testament to the developers' ability to stay true to the identity of the game even when making significant changes to the specific expression. I'm pretty confident the Changeling team will be able to do the same here.<br /> <br /> As to your specific concerns regarding &quot;ways for a clever player to exemplify the theme of beautiful madness and build the character they truly wanted to play&quot;, YMMV, but from my perspective it looks like a lot of the mechanical changes are being made specifically to expand the ways for players to play the character they want to play. With Seeming being divorced from Kith, over 100 Kiths to choose from and options for creating your own unique Kith, Clarity Breaking Points being highly personalized, a system for creating custom Courts and Freeholds... 2e is looking more customizable and personalizable than 1e ever was, which is saying a lot.<br /> <br /> I think the biggest thing that's going to make the difference between players who adopt 2e and the players who stick with 1e is going to be that &quot;beautiful madness&quot; part. 2e does seem to be shifting away from that theme towards &quot;beautiful lies and terrible truths&quot;, and for some that may be too dramatic of a departure. To me, the latter is just a more mature expression of the same ideas the former speaks to, but I've heard from others who disagree. Hopefully the end result is satisfying to many existing fans and brings in new ones to boot, but if you find you and yours would rather stick with 1e, that's a valid option as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T14:33:33-07:00","id":967525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=962354#post962354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know man, Werewolf had some significant changes both to mechanics and to the setting. The Gifts system was completely restructured, Rites got their own completely new system, Harmony was re-built from the ground up to focus on balancing between extremes, Kuruth got significantly expanded upon and the system for determining Kuruth triggers was changed as well, Lunacy was divorced from Willpower and tied into the Breaking Point system and split into three different Conditions (four with the right Gift Facet), the Tribes were changed from roles in werewolf society to organizations founded on common sacred prey, Unahir were excised from the game... The fact that it still feels quintessentially <i>Werewolf the Forsaken</i>, that anyone could look at the two editions side by side and say they were &quot;mostly the same game with minor updates and adjustments&quot; is a testament to the developers' ability to stay true to the identity of the game even when making significant changes to the specific expression. I'm pretty confident the Changeling team will be able to do the same here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shrug. Maybe Werewolf has fewer sacred cows for me. Or maybe I was just expecting most of those adjustments. As far Gifts go, the basic concept stays the same regardless of the system being different (same as Contracts I suppose, but then again the changes to Contracts don't bother me to much). Rites weren't really what got me into werewolf and only got emphasized when the players showed interest or it just felt illogical not to address them- never went out of my way to use them so I have no vested interest in them getting changed around. And yeah, Lunacy got a face lift and expansion but the core concept is still there just with more variety. And Harmony was to be expected to keep up with the changes done to the Morality system in 2nd edition. Frankly it was a neat way to reflect the man vs animal theme in Werewolf and a rather original way to play with the system where being very high on the scale was just as detrimental as being very low rather than the straight up and down top=saint, bottom=psycho we were expecting. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=962354#post962354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to your specific concerns regarding &quot;ways for a clever player to exemplify the theme of beautiful madness and build the character they truly wanted to play&quot;, YMMV, but from my perspective it looks like a lot of the mechanical changes are being made specifically to expand the ways for players to play the character they want to play. With Seeming being divorced from Kith, over 100 Kiths to choose from and options for creating your own unique Kith, Clarity Breaking Points being highly personalized, a system for creating custom Courts and Freeholds... 2e is looking more customizable and personalizable than 1e ever was, which is saying a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I couldn't disagree more in that regard. Yeah, some new aspects are opening up (Anchors look promising) but other aspects are getting locked down HARD this edition. Or so the snippets we've seen are suggesting to me. Pledges seem to have fallen under some kind of role-playing martial law- who you can make them with, what benefits you can derive, the penalities for breaking them- the system frankly feels gutted and stripped down way beyond whatever might have been necessary to combat power gamers or whatever the original concern was. Making Hollow has gotten less fun- while some portions of the merit have been nicely streamlined (defenses and such) other cool features are totally absent and it makes me sad (for instance, you used to have several doorways exist between the Hollow and the mortal world...now I can't tell from the text if a Hollow is even allowed ANY connection to the real world). Making Tokens doesn't as versatile as it was. Dreamwalking hasn't necessarily gotten less free...but remember what I said about sacred cows? Dancers in the Dusk is probably my favorite book from the whole line, so despite the multiple nods to the dream chapter in that book I feel like Skein-walking has by necessity gotten booted out of existence in place of this Dream Bastion stuff. Which is...meh. Luke warm on the concept of dreamers minds entering the Hedge while they sleep (I preferred keeping the relationship between dreams and Hedge more ambigious, frankly). And changelings shifting physically into the Hedge when they &quot;sleep&quot;? That's a bizarre change to me and drastically alters when and why you would do Dreamwalking in significant ways (I mean, for example, if you know a True Fae is invading a dream the usual response would be to leap in and help the mortal- which previously the players would do without hesitation- but FUCK if they would be willing to disturb a dream if it risks popping the sleeper awake and leaving them sitting in the middle of the Thorns eye to eye with an angry Keeper!!). Just not a fan, at least with the limited information I currently have to go by.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=962354#post962354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the biggest thing that's going to make the difference between players who adopt 2e and the players who stick with 1e is going to be that &quot;beautiful madness&quot; part. 2e does seem to be shifting away from that theme towards &quot;beautiful lies and terrible truths&quot;, and for some that may be too dramatic of a departure. To me, the latter is just a more mature expression of the same ideas the former speaks to, but I've heard from others who disagree. Hopefully the end result is satisfying to many existing fans and brings in new ones to boot, but if you find you and yours would rather stick with 1e, that's a valid option as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm not wowed by the end result I'll most likely just take the new bits I like and plug them back into the 1e system. I won't gun for every Changeling book in 2e this time, I'm sure. But I doubt wild horses could keep me away from the Hedge book, at the very least. Partly because wild horses would have a hard time messing with my internet connection to Drivethrurpg, but mostly because I'm a sucker for anything hedge related.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T15:17:32-07:00","id":967553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=967525#post967525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shrug. Maybe Werewolf has fewer sacred cows for me. Or maybe I was just expecting most of those adjustments. As far Gifts go, the basic concept stays the same regardless of the system being different (same as Contracts I suppose, but then again the changes to Contracts don't bother me to much). Rites weren't really what got me into werewolf and only got emphasized when the players showed interest or it just felt illogical not to address them- never went out of my way to use them so I have no vested interest in them getting changed around. And yeah, Lunacy got a face lift and expansion but the core concept is still there just with more variety. And Harmony was to be expected to keep up with the changes done to the Morality system in 2nd edition. Frankly it was a neat way to reflect the man vs animal theme in Werewolf and a rather original way to play with the system where being very high on the scale was just as detrimental as being very low rather than the straight up and down top=saint, bottom=psycho we were expecting.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't deny though that it's more than some minor updates. There are a lot of differences, and the above is only talking mechanics. There were some huge story changes too, like Tribes being changed from societal roles to organizations built around a common sacred prey, the concept of Pack being expanded to include wolf blooded and humans, the Flock Must Not Know being significantly relaxed to allow for the above, the removal of Unahair and along with it the taboos about werewolf-on-werewolf mating, and the re-focusing of pretty much everything to emphasize the need to hunt over the sacred duty to protect the boarder between the spirit and the flesh. Any of those things could have been sacred cows for some fans, and in fact I recall hearing a lot of protestations of &quot;the Forsaken don't feel very Forsaken any more&quot; as criticism of several of the above points shortly after the release of 2e. Personally I think they were all changes for the better, but they don't seem any less significant to me than the changes to Changeling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=967525#post967525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I couldn't disagree more in that regard. Yeah, some new aspects are opening up (Anchors look promising) but other aspects are getting locked down HARD this edition. Or so the snippets we've seen are suggesting to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see anywhere that is happening in terms of character customization options. But, I guess it's a pretty subjective thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=967525#post967525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pledges seem to have fallen under some kind of role-playing martial law- who you can make them with, what benefits you can derive, the penalities for breaking them- the system frankly feels gutted and stripped down way beyond whatever might have been necessary to combat power gamers or whatever the original concern was.</div> </div> </div> </div>2e Pledges seem to me like an entirely different thing than 1e Pledges. The role 1e Pledges filled seems to have been taken over by the Goblin Vow Merit. Which, granted, is not quite as potent as 1e pledges, but seems to me to have a similar level of customization. Just with more limited scope, which I don't really see as a bad thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=967525#post967525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making Hollow has gotten less fun- while some portions of the merit have been nicely streamlined (defenses and such) other cool features are totally absent and it makes me sad (for instance, you used to have several doorways exist between the Hollow and the mortal world...now I can't tell from the text if a Hollow is even allowed ANY connection to the real world).</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Hollow seems pretty much the same to me. I mean, it's not 3 different Merits any more, but that's par for the course with 2e, Haven was streamlined in the same way. Yes, they still are connected to Ironside, usually via a door, And I thought multiple Doors was one of the potential perks you could get with Hollow dots? I think it was called Easy Access, or something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=967525#post967525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making Tokens doesn't as versatile as it was.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't think we had seen the Token rules yet?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=967525#post967525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dreamwalking hasn't necessarily gotten less free...but remember what I said about sacred cows? Dancers in the Dusk is probably my favorite book from the whole line, so despite the multiple nods to the dream chapter in that book I feel like Skein-walking has by necessity gotten booted out of existence in place of this Dream Bastion stuff. Which is...meh. Luke warm on the concept of dreamers minds entering the Hedge while they sleep (I preferred keeping the relationship between dreams and Hedge more ambigious, frankly). And changelings shifting physically into the Hedge when they &amp;quot;sleep&amp;quot;? That's a bizarre change to me and drastically alters when and why you would do Dreamwalking in significant ways (I mean, for example, if you know a True Fae is invading a dream the usual response would be to leap in and help the mortal- which previously the players would do without hesitation- but FUCK if they would be willing to disturb a dream if it risks popping the sleeper awake and leaving them sitting in the middle of the Thorns eye to eye with an angry Keeper!!). Just not a fan, at least with the limited information I currently have to go by.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fair critique, although it isn't really about customization. Personally, I vastly prefer dreams being actual physical locations in the Hedge over 1e's take which were too ambiguous for my taste. But yeah, it's one of those changes on the order of the way the concept of Pack was changed for werewolf, and it's one of those things people will love or hate. On the subject of Changelings physically entering the Hedge in their sleep, I don't think that's quite how it works. They can either remain physically in Ironside and not dream, or they can physically enter their own dream, because Changelings treat dreams as physical spaces in 2e. I'm actually not sure if Changelings' dreams create Dream Bastions in the Hedge or not though, they very well might.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=967525#post967525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm not wowed by the end result I'll most likely just take the new bits I like and plug them back into the 1e system. I won't gun for every Changeling book in 2e this time, I'm sure. But I doubt wild horses could keep me away from the Hedge book, at the very least. Partly because wild horses would have a hard time messing with my internet connection to Drivethrurpg, but mostly because I'm a sucker for anything hedge related.</div> </div> </div> </div>All perfectly reasonable. Cheers, friend!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T18:38:38-07:00","id":968292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=962354#post962354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know man, Werewolf had some significant changes both to mechanics and to the setting. The Gifts system was completely restructured, Rites got their own completely new system, Harmony was re-built from the ground up to focus on balancing between extremes, Kuruth got significantly expanded upon and the system for determining Kuruth triggers was changed as well, Lunacy was divorced from Willpower and tied into the Breaking Point system and split into three different Conditions (four with the right Gift Facet), the Tribes were changed from roles in werewolf society to organizations founded on common sacred prey, Unahir were excised from the game... The fact that it still feels quintessentially <i>Werewolf the Forsaken</i>, that anyone could look at the two editions side by side and say they were &quot;mostly the same game with minor updates and adjustments&quot; is a testament to the developers' ability to stay true to the identity of the game even when making significant changes to the specific expression. I'm pretty confident the Changeling team will be able to do the same here.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my experience, while i like Werewolf the forsaken, 1st edition was dragging a lot of corpses of Apocalypse (Social rites, weird scaling gifts, metis-like-being, etc etc) so the makeover of 2nd edition didnt felt that bad. On the other hand changeling was a pretty solid game with only dream walking being the Dreaming corpse it carried.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=962354#post962354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the biggest thing that's going to make the difference between players who adopt 2e and the players who stick with 1e is going to be that &quot;beautiful madness&quot; part. 2e does seem to be shifting away from that theme towards &quot;beautiful lies and terrible truths&quot;, and for some that may be too dramatic of a departure. To me, the latter is just a more mature expression of the same ideas the former speaks to, but I've heard from others who disagree. Hopefully the end result is satisfying to many existing fans and brings in new ones to boot, but if you find you and yours would rather stick with 1e, that's a valid option as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont know about that, the little tagline under each game has always being a lie in some way or another and i see more people drifting from 1ed or 2nd on whether they prefer to play a established &quot;setting&quot; (1st) or those who want to do all the work themselves and make courts/freehold model from 0 (2nd). I find myself on the 1st edition camp so far.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=962354#post962354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't think we had seen the Token rules yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>We have never see Token rules period. I dont know what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2244\" data-vbnamecard=\"2244\">nothri</a> is talking about, i never saw rules for making token in 1st edition either.<br /> <br /> There were rule for making hedgespun item that were the equivalent of +1 sword/armor and authomatons but making tokens? No rule for that. And the rules for hedge spun couldnt exactly be used for tokens as for one hedgespun had very specific effects contrary to tokens and it didnt took into account the drawbacks that token suffered so one was forced to eyeball it and let the DM (who had no guideline except the example tokens to compare) decide or just pick the example tokens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 09-12-2016, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T20:17:01-07:00","id":968331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=968292#post968292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont know about that, the little tagline under each game has always being a lie in some way or another and i see more people drifting from 1ed or 2nd on whether they prefer to play a established &amp;quot;setting&amp;quot; (1st) or those who want to do all the work themselves and make courts/freehold model from 0 (2nd). I find myself on the 1st edition camp so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do know you can just use the seasonal courts in 2e if you want, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T20:35:31-07:00","id":968338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=967553#post967553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. Hollow seems pretty much the same to me. I mean, it's not 3 different Merits any more, but that's par for the course with 2e, Haven was streamlined in the same way. Yes, they still are connected to Ironside, usually via a door, And I thought multiple Doors was one of the potential perks you could get with Hollow dots? I think it was called Easy Access, or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Easy Access is &quot;the Hollow has no consistent Earthly access point because you can access it from anywhere, just like the Bolthole perk of the same name.&quot;<br /> <br /> Escape Route gives you a one-way exit that comes out some distance from the entrance \u2014 though the nature of the 1e Doors 0 state of a Hollow contributes some ambiguity, the fact that it comes out at a predetermined location and a Huntsman waiting outside the entrance to your Hollow is one of the explicit reasons the perk has its uses suggests to me that the emergency hatch comes out on Earth.<br /> <br /> Size Matters 2 can easily give you a Hollow big enough that successfully opening a new Hedge gate is a trivial means of adding new entrances (and swiss-cheesing your security, but that's a concern that 1e didn't have outside the context of needing to opt into Hollow Wards). <br /> <br /> (Two of our playtest characters have personal Hollows, getting one is the long-term Aspiration of a third, and the plot of the current arc of WUtB basically revolves around fae real-estate brokerage. Magical housing development is something I keep in mind.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T13:36:41-07:00","id":968707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=968331#post968331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do know you can just use the seasonal courts in 2e if you want, right?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And others, Toronto and Honshu are both spoiled. I don't remember if there were others.<br /> <br /> It's not like they aren't including samples ones that you can just use as is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T14:24:24-07:00","id":968739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=968331#post968331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do know you can just use the seasonal courts in 2e if you want, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the other 2nd editions are any indication the way they gonna do it is introduce new element/change old ones but not explain the minutia of how that affect the setting and letting each dm make that call or just use broad strokes like in mage 2nd edition inuring was introduce but not the views of each order on something that basically bypass the morality system.<br /> <br /> Some people like to make the setting from scratch other prefer to work within the limits impose by a setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 09-13-2016, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T14:34:32-07:00","id":968745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=968739#post968739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the other 2nd editions are any indication the way they gonna do it is introduce new element/change old ones but not explain the minutia of how that affect the setting and letting each dm make that call</div> </div> </div> </div>In what way do you imagine this is an obstacle to &quot;the Seasonal Courts keep the Fae away by voluntarily handing over rulership of the freehold as the year goes on&quot;?<br /> <br /> At worst you might have to rejigger the Mantle allocations from whatever sample setting uses them to better suit the locale your game takes place in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T15:12:52-07:00","id":968769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=968745#post968745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In what way do you imagine this is an obstacle to &quot;the Seasonal Courts keep the Fae away by voluntarily handing over rulership of the freehold as the year goes on&quot;?<br /> <br /> At worst you might have to rejigger the Mantle allocations from whatever sample setting uses them to better suit the locale your game takes place in.</div> </div> </div> </div>First we dont have the book yet so i dont know yet whats gonna conflict with what. However as i said if 2nd edition is any indication any change is gonna just be throw up there without explaining how is gonna affect the setting. Inuring in mage, the powerup lunar gift and depowering of the pure while not explaining how they still are the &quot;winning side&quot;.<br /> <br /> For example i dont like to have to rejigger the mantle allocations, i preffer that the summer court is the summer court no matter the location than having the player expectative of making personalize court for a location and neither i like to have to fiddle with mechanics and worry that certain election of mantle is OP. I also dont like that one can choose the court contracts.<br /> <br /> So my point is that i disagree with Charlaquin when she says that the main thing is gonna separate people sticking with 1st or 2nd edition is whether they preffer the theme of &quot;beautiful madness&quot; or &quot;sweet lies and terrible truths&quot;<br /> <br /> I never saw changeling 1st edition acomplishing beautiful madness part but neither i saw Werewolf acomplishing savage fury nor mage &quot;mordern sorcery&quot; I like the 3 games but the that little taglines was meaningless.<br /> <br /> So my take is that whether people stick with 1st or 2nd is more to do with whether they find the new elements appealing (huntsmen, the more narrative approach to everything, superforms, pledges, etc) and whether they preffer to customize each freehold from scratch (determing bulwark, determing rituals, determining ideals &amp; emotion, determing courts, determining contracts for said courts) to match the location or they prefer to use the setting as written.<br /> <br /> Example i live in a coast city with a harsh winter and a busy summer. So if i were using second edition i could create the court of desolation, fish, salt and tourism to match the cycle my city goes through. Or if im using 1st just use the seasonal courts and think how they might fit in that locale without changing the courts. I prefer the second option as DM i have too many thing to keep track off than having to create and balance new stuff. I personally think that 1st edition is more a setting-in-a-can kind of game while second edition is gonna be the more &quot;bucket of legos&quot; kind of game of all 2nd edition from the previews so far.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T17:12:54-07:00","id":968838,"title":"","content":"I'm an Australian, if we tried to use seasonal courts we'd just end up with the summer court and then the gentry would all murder the changelings since there is no other court to swap over control to. Also... there were other courts like the directional courts and that light based one. So... it's not really any change in the setting that different locations have different courts.<br /> <br /> In 1e it was &quot;Okay we're assuming you're using the seasonal courts... but other places sorta might have different things but you're going to have to make up tonnes of mechanics for them with no real guidelines beyond three examples. Good luck&quot;, in 2e you get &quot;You can have the seasonal courts, directional courts, colour courts, whatever courts fit your freehold, here is how you do it in a few easy steps&quot;....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 09-13-2016, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T17:19:37-07:00","id":968844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=968838#post968838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm an Australian, if we tried to use seasonal courts we'd just end up with the summer court and then the gentry would all murder the changelings since there is no other court to swap over control to. Also... there were other courts like the directional courts and that light based one. So... it's not really any change in the setting that different locations have different courts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Theres a difference between &quot;here is this set number of courts and how they work&quot; and &quot;here is a system to make your own courts&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T17:28:35-07:00","id":968848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=968844#post968844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Theres a difference between &quot;here is this set number of courts and how they work&quot; and &quot;here is a system to make your own courts&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except the set courts are still there, they are just not assumed to be the only ones in every place from the get go. and they ALSO are including rules for making your own. The seasonal courts being a 'sample' doesn't make them less usable as a generic court if you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T17:34:14-07:00","id":968850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=968844#post968844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Theres a difference between &quot;here is this set number of courts and how they work&quot; and &quot;here is a system to make your own courts&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the second is much more useful considering the courts that were provided aren't wide enough to cover the immense variety of different cultures and locations on the planet (page count required to attempt A that covers tonnes of cultures would be ridiculous), and the fact that it still has all the benefits of A. The set number of courts was far too low. And note that those set number of courts wasn't the number of different court types in the setting, it's just that they were the courts they showed not that those courts were all the courts on the planet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T18:02:55-07:00","id":968872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=968838#post968838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm an Australian, if we tried to use seasonal courts we'd just end up with the summer court and then the gentry would all murder the changelings since there is no other court to swap over control to. Also... there were other courts like the directional courts and that light based one. So... it's not really any change in the setting that different locations have different courts.<br /> <br /> In 1e it was &quot;Okay we're assuming you're using the seasonal courts... but other places sorta might have different things but you're going to have to make up tonnes of mechanics for them with no real guidelines beyond three examples. Good luck&quot;, in 2e you get &quot;You can have the seasonal courts, directional courts, colour courts, whatever courts fit your freehold, here is how you do it in a few easy steps&quot;....</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I think maybe some people consider it a setting thing, but I think the biggest difference is that in 1e, somewhere about 95% of the page count of the game assumed you were playing with the four Amero-Euro-Assumptive Seasonal Courts. Now, except for the pages literally talking about the freehold using them, none of the pages assume you're using them. <br /> <br /> I think the Seasonal Courts worked as a shorthand for some concepts, it helped some players jump in. But I also think it felt distant and arbitrary to others. I found some of the other courts fascinating, but because of the 1e style of supplementary material, none could ever really get much attention. I felt that was a lost opportunity. (Lost opportunity. See what I did there?) <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T18:14:43-07:00","id":968878,"title":"","content":"Can someone remind who what the settings are in the new core?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T18:21:46-07:00","id":968882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=968850#post968850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, the second is much more useful considering the courts that were provided aren't wide enough to cover the immense variety of different cultures and locations on the planet (page count required to attempt A that covers tonnes of cultures would be ridiculous), and the fact that it still has all the benefits of A. The set number of courts was far too low. And note that those set number of courts wasn't the number of different court types in the setting, it's just that they were the courts they showed not that those courts were all the courts on the planet.</div> </div> </div> </div>And thats why you would probably like 2nd edition more, while i, unless something really impress me, will stick with the &quot;settting-in-a-can&quot; of 1st.<br /> <br /> Courts aside personally i seems little to like in 2nd. Fae touched became unecesary convoluted, the whole focus on the narrative of the courts is something im not sure about, all court gain the contract to tale spinning which i dont know if it has anything to do with the talespinning mechanic of 1st which i didnt like so im neutral there.<br /> <br /> I get what they did for the huntsmen and why but it still feel like an unecesary middleman and a pretty invasive element.<br /> <br /> The focus on dream is something i dont care about, it felt like an uncesary element in 1st edition already. And the new forms feel like an unecesary add on.<br /> <br /> Fortunately i still have 1st as a pretty complete game and its one of those game which crossover dimish the game so i dont have worry about using the 2e of other lines <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 09-13-2016, 09:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T19:34:03-07:00","id":968929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=968878#post968878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone remind who what the settings are in the new core?</div> </div> </div> </div>The final version is going to have:<br /> <br /> Toronto<br /> Paris<br /> Miami<br /> Tokyo<br /> <br /> We planned to have a couple more, but writing fell through on those, and I decided the words would be better spent fleshing out a couple of other game concepts, like the Hedge.<br /> <br /> THAT SAID, I have plans for more settings upcoming. And hopefully on a relatively short timeline. I have some plans for the Directional Courts, but I have to make a few moving pieces fall together right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T19:49:06-07:00","id":968941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=968929#post968929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The final version is going to have:<br /> <br /> Toronto<br /> Paris<br /> Miami<br /> Tokyo<br /> <br /> We planned to have a couple more, but writing fell through on those, and I decided the words would be better spent fleshing out a couple of other game concepts, like the Hedge.<br /> <br /> THAT SAID, I have plans for more settings upcoming. And hopefully on a relatively short timeline. I have some plans for the Directional Courts, but I have to make a few moving pieces fall together right.</div> </div> </div> </div>So we've seen Tokyo and Toronto's Courts, and Miami is reprising the Seasonal... I'm intensely curious what Paris will bring to the table, especially with my rough plans to merge Pelgrane Press' <i>Dreamhounds of Paris</i> (a historical Cthulhu frame where you play as the major figures of the Surrealist movement) with Changeling somehow. If you're taking requests, I'd kill to see the Directional Courts make a return in a Hong Kong setting, and I certainly wouldn't mind having a hand in writing such a thing!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T19:55:28-07:00","id":968944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=968929#post968929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The final version is going to have:<br /> <br /> Toronto<br /> Paris<br /> Miami<br /> Tokyo<br /> <br /> We planned to have a couple more, but writing fell through on those, and I decided the words would be better spent fleshing out a couple of other game concepts, like the Hedge.<br /> <br /> THAT SAID, I have plans for more settings upcoming. And hopefully on a relatively short timeline. I have some plans for the Directional Courts, but I have to make a few moving pieces fall together right.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could probably write a book on new kiths or freeholds. Have you considered pitching an idea for a book with both submitted by fans? If a writer submits a freehold and a kith or two that might be enough word count worth some money. It would certainly be enough for a writing sample with plenty of fluff and crunch to make an assessment. Seems like writers are the bottleneck for publishing. Maybe it would be worth making a book just to find a few new writers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T20:33:33-07:00","id":968962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=968941#post968941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So we've seen Tokyo and Toronto's Courts, and Miami is reprising the Seasonal... I'm intensely curious what Paris will bring to the table, especially with my rough plans to merge Pelgrane Press' <i>Dreamhounds of Paris</i> (a historical Cthulhu frame where you play as the major figures of the Surrealist movement) with Changeling somehow. If you're taking requests, I'd kill to see the Directional Courts make a return in a Hong Kong setting, and I certainly wouldn't mind having a hand in writing such a thing!</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, during Dev ArcaneArts has been added to the Changeling team, and they were working on a Court system set up in Paris called the Rose Courts. I mean, I'm not sure, but it'd make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T20:39:10-07:00","id":968965,"title":"","content":"Something I don't understand about the &quot;setting-in-a-can&quot; thing, why don't 2e games count as having those? Each one has a selection of &quot;settings-in-a-can&quot; that you can easily grab and use rather than having to make one up yourself. Or am I misunderstanding that aspect of the issue?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T20:42:11-07:00","id":968966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=968962#post968962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, during Dev ArcaneArts has been added to the Changeling team, and they were working on a Court system set up in Paris called the Rose Courts. I mean, I'm not sure, but it'd make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure you're not thinking of the Rose Courts that wound up in Elizabethan London, in Dark Eras? <br /> <br /> I wonder if those are still around in the modern day, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 09-13-2016, 11:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T21:06:26-07:00","id":968982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=968962#post968962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, during Dev ArcaneArts has been added to the Changeling team, and they were working on a Court system set up in Paris called the Rose Courts. I mean, I'm not sure, but it'd make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Actually, I was hiring ArcaneArts for some stuff later down the line, but I had space for a setting. So, I talked about getting Paris in there. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=968944#post968944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could probably write a book on new kiths or freeholds. Have you considered pitching an idea for a book with both submitted by fans? If a writer submits a freehold and a kith or two that might be enough word count worth some money. It would certainly be enough for a writing sample with plenty of fluff and crunch to make an assessment. Seems like writers are the bottleneck for publishing. Maybe it would be worth making a book just to find a few new writers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, that'd be challenging. Lots of moving parts. Also, I know the one time we tried something like that, Bloodlines: The Chosen, it was a less than ideal situation all around. <br /> <br /> And I assure you, writers are not a bottleneck for us really. We have plenty of writing talent. <br /> <br /> I've got some cool plans for Lost 2E. Let's see where those go. I'd really like to do a Courts book. It's not currently in the works. But, it'd be one of my first big things to pitch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=968941#post968941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So we've seen Tokyo and Toronto's Courts, and Miami is reprising the Seasonal... I'm intensely curious what Paris will bring to the table, especially with my rough plans to merge Pelgrane Press' <i>Dreamhounds of Paris</i> (a historical Cthulhu frame where you play as the major figures of the Surrealist movement) with Changeling somehow. If you're taking requests, I'd kill to see the Directional Courts make a return in a Hong Kong setting, and I certainly wouldn't mind having a hand in writing such a thing!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not CURRENTLY looking. I THINK I have someone in mind. But I've got to figure out a couple of things first. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T21:09:46-07:00","id":968985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=968966#post968966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you sure you're not thinking of the Rose Courts that wound up in Elizabethan London, in Dark Eras?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=552287#post552287\">the</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=554492#post554492\">Rosiere</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=559072#post559072\">is definitely</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=572106#post572106\">Paris</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T21:13:14-07:00","id":968990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=968985#post968985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=552287#post552287\">the</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=554492#post554492\">Rosiere</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=559072#post559072\">is definitely</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=572106#post572106\">Paris</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies for getting confused. That'll happen with two Rose Courts running around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T21:29:44-07:00","id":968998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=968982#post968982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, that'd be challenging. Lots of moving parts. Also, I know the one time we tried something like that, Bloodlines: The Chosen, it was a less than ideal situation all around.<br /> <br /> And I assure you, writers are not a bottleneck for us really. We have plenty of writing talent.<br /> <br /> I've got some cool plans for Lost 2E. Let's see where those go. I'd really like to do a Courts book. It's not currently in the works. But, it'd be one of my first big things to pitch.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I thought you were looking into something like that. Makes no difference to me as I'm not a writer. After a Hedge book, a Court book seems logical. It would go well with that Crossover book so maybe that would be a good time to go for it. Good luck. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T22:36:23-07:00","id":969028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=968990#post968990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Apologies for getting confused. That'll happen with two Rose Courts running around.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally asked around to see if two Rose Courts was going to be a problem, but the Rosiere is totally fine.<br /> <br /> Can't wait for you all to see the final revised version, but with only four settings instead of five, it'll probably have to wait for the release-not that a lot of it isn't up on the forums anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T22:39:29-07:00","id":969029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=969028#post969028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I totally asked around to see if two Rose Courts was going to be a problem, but the Rosiere is totally fine.<br /> <br /> Can't wait for you all to see the final revised version, but with only four settings instead of five, it'll probably have to wait for the release-not that a lot of it isn't up on the forums anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking forward to it! The settings are my favorite parts of the 2e cores.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T00:04:39-07:00","id":969061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=944918#post944918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bear in mind that Changeling tricks won't work on cold iron. You can still hold them with a properly constructed prison, or find a way to reduce their glamour to zero (thorns from the hedge should do), both of which were good practices even before 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would that work actually?<br /> I've seen this problem too with the lack of any proper way to capture and hold people.<br /> IE: You are two changeling courtiers told to go on patrol in the city and suddenly you spot a Changeling you've never seen before. You tell them to stop - They could be a threat to security, and they run for it.<br /> <br /> To actually grab them and hold them is more or less impossible unless you beat the crap out of them.<br /> <br /> But now that you mentioned it actually... Wouldn't a pair of at least 50% iron cuffs be enough?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whatever its origin, iron that is at least half pure ignores fae-born defenses and magic. </div> </div> </div>With that wording, I'd judge it as trying to slip free from iron-bonds are impossible. You wouldn't need cold iron, that's an overkill (although it could be useful to reduce chances of any other magical attempts of escape).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T02:45:10-07:00","id":969109,"title":"","content":"Escaping a grapple with another Changeling is a Clash of Wills, so their odds of slipping free are probably far from guaranteed, and they only have so much glamour to burn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T04:36:03-07:00","id":969142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=968965#post968965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I don't understand about the &quot;setting-in-a-can&quot; thing, why don't 2e games count as having those? Each one has a selection of &quot;settings-in-a-can&quot; that you can easily grab and use rather than having to make one up yourself. Or am I misunderstanding that aspect of the issue?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the gamelines for starters, i didnt say Setting-in-a-can was something of 1st edition, i said 1st edition changeling.<br /> <br /> 1st edition Werewolf and mage had pretty big holes in their setting that expected Dm to fill in. How the concilium and uratha politics works was horribly explained from werewolf tendency of treating each pack as its own island but them throwing elements that could only exist on an organized scheme to mage attempt that boiled down to just throw options after options without explaining how said options interact with each other.<br /> <br /> A perfect example of setting in a can is Werewolf the apocalypse whose setting was clearly define. This is the tribes, this is how they interact, this is how they resolve disputes, this is how they and why they get more rank. This is the positions of their septs, etc etc. Very few elements were not given a &quot;canon&quot; answer, as a dm i could always change whatever i didnt like but i had that canon answer to fall back or as a base to work from.<br /> <br /> Same with changeling<br /> This are the courts, this is the party line for resolving conflicts, this the positions, etc etc. They even manage, though very very clumsily, stablish the political importance of the motley. The courts have a non-local history to them, making each court localize and its history start and finish in its own location feels mundane to me, i know personal taste but i like when the organizations surpass the locations and i preffer having to adapt a group to a court and thus show a establish court under a new light than than making up a court that perfectly fits them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=968982#post968982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, that'd be challenging. Lots of moving parts. Also, I know the one time we tried something like that, Bloodlines: The Chosen, it was a less than ideal situation all around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im curious what was the problem with bloodlines the choosen?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T05:17:26-07:00","id":969153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=969142#post969142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Im curious what was the problem with bloodlines the choosen?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just logistically very, very challenging. While being a very small book, it was a ton of work. And it was hard to find enough serviceable drafts that weren't just overlapping copies of the same bloodlines, or covering the same conceptual space. <br /> <br /> It's always hard to work with a big team. It's even harder when they're not seasoned writers. It's even harder when they're not involved intimately with development, and given strong direction from the outset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T05:39:18-07:00","id":969162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=969142#post969142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the clarification.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Same with changeling<br /> This are the courts, this is the party line for resolving conflicts, this the positions, etc etc. They even manage, though very very clumsily, stablish the political importance of the motley. The courts have a non-local history to them, making each court localize and its history start and finish in its own location feels mundane to me, i know personal taste but i like when the organizations surpass the locations and i preffer having to adapt a group to a court and thus show a establish court under a new light than than making up a court that perfectly fits them. </div> </div> </div>Good. The 2e court system does what you want then.<br /> <br /> The seasonal court is still there that you can apply to tonnes of locations. The court creation rules have the general ones like Seasonal as ones that can basically apply to Any location OR you could have one that's specific to the locale. What your talking about is an option in the Court Creation rules that we have been given. It says &quot;The story is something familiar; like the Celtic myths of the seelie and unseelie, or seasonal courts. Or it might be something more regionally specific &quot; Note the &quot;or&quot;. Seasonal Courts are listed as a specific example of a story that applies to tonnes of regions so people like you don't need to use the regionally specific courts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T06:57:57-07:00","id":969200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=969162#post969162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good. The 2e court system does what you want then.<br /> <br /> The seasonal court is still there that you can apply to tonnes of locations. The court creation rules have the general ones like Seasonal as ones that can basically apply to Any location OR you could have one that's specific to the locale. What your talking about is an option in the Court Creation rules that we have been given. It says &quot;The story is something familiar; like the Celtic myths of the seelie and unseelie, or seasonal courts. Or it might be something more regionally specific &quot; Note the &quot;or&quot;. Seasonal Courts are listed as a specific example of a story that applies to tonnes of regions so people like you don't need to use the regionally specific courts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be honestly, when the book is out i will give it a chance.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T08:28:29-07:00","id":969238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=968929#post968929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The final version is going to have:<br /> <br /> Toronto<br /> Paris<br /> Miami<br /> Tokyo<br /> <br /> We planned to have a couple more, but writing fell through on those, and I decided the words would be better spent fleshing out a couple of other game concepts, like the Hedge.<br /> <br /> THAT SAID, I have plans for more settings upcoming. And hopefully on a relatively short timeline. I have some plans for the Directional Courts, but I have to make a few moving pieces fall together right.</div> </div> </div> </div> I find it interesting that the Settings are bigger then the settings in 2e Requiem, 2e Mage, 2e Promeathan.<br /> <br /> Toronto, Miami, and Toyko are all really big (I've only seen Toyko and Toronto, but Miami was the core setting in 1e, so it seems obvious).<br /> <br /> I figure even Paris will be reasonable big, if the others are any indication.<br /> <br /> You have 5 courts in Roserie Courts, 4-5 Courts in 1001 Nights Toronto Freehold (plus two smaller Freeholds, seasonal and seelie), Toyko has 3 Moon Princess Courts, and 4 Seasonal Courts in Miami.<br /> <br /> That 17 individual courts to be detailed, including mechanics court contracts, mantle, various merits, bulwark, approaches, court story, court symbols/colours/ranks, court fluff, ect....<br /> <br /> Then each setting has important locations like the CN Tower for example.<br /> <br /> It has a History, plothooks, local weirdness, Huntsmen, and other assorted elements.<br /> <br /> So I think they're bigger word count wise, and that doesn't include more universal Hedge elements in the Hedge section.<br /> <br /> One place I'd love to see done later in another book is Khajuraho in India.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 09-14-2016, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T09:02:29-07:00","id":969251,"title":"","content":"The OP could mix the 1e and 2e elements that the OP prefers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T17:56:11-07:00","id":969566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=969238#post969238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find it interesting that the Settings are bigger then the settings in 2e Requiem, 2e Mage, 2e Promeathan.<br /> <br /> Toronto, Miami, and Toyko are all really big (I've only seen Toyko and Toronto, but Miami was the core setting in 1e, so it seems obvious).<br /> <br /> I figure even Paris will be reasonable big, if the others are any indication.<br /> <br /> You have 5 courts in Roserie Courts, 4-5 Courts in 1001 Nights Toronto Freehold (plus two smaller Freeholds, seasonal and seelie), Toyko has 3 Moon Princess Courts, and 4 Seasonal Courts in Miami.<br /> <br /> That 17 individual courts to be detailed, including mechanics court contracts, mantle, various merits, bulwark, approaches, court story, court symbols/colours/ranks, court fluff, ect....<br /> <br /> Then each setting has important locations like the CN Tower for example.<br /> <br /> It has a History, plothooks, local weirdness, Huntsmen, and other assorted elements.<br /> <br /> So I think they're bigger word count wise, and that doesn't include more universal Hedge elements in the Hedge section.<br /> <br /> One place I'd love to see done later in another book is Khajuraho in India.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are bigger. In fact, this Tokyo one is the biggest I think we've gotten so far in general (if you don't count Hurt Locker's, which is different in a lot of ways). And the reason I did this was because of the new Court-crafting system. I wanted to make sure people had diverse plug-and-play settings they could work with if they didn't want to build their own.<br /> <br /> My goal would also be to include at least one or two in any supplements we do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T18:29:54-07:00","id":969579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=969566#post969566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are bigger. In fact, this Tokyo one is the biggest I think we've gotten so far in general (if you don't count Hurt Locker's, which is different in a lot of ways). And the reason I did this was because of the new Court-crafting system. I wanted to make sure people had diverse plug-and-play settings they could work with if they didn't want to build their own.<br /> <br /> My goal would also be to include at least one or two in any supplements we do.</div> </div> </div> </div>awesome! have you decided which courts will appear in the Hedge? perhaps Seelie &amp; Unseelie?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T18:45:20-07:00","id":969585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=969238#post969238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find it interesting that the Settings are bigger then the settings in 2e Requiem, 2e Mage, 2e Promeathan.<br /> <br /> Toronto, Miami, and Toyko are all really big (I've only seen Toyko and Toronto, but Miami was the core setting in 1e, so it seems obvious).<br /> <br /> I figure even Paris will be reasonable big, if the others are any indication.<br /> <br /> You have 5 courts in Roserie Courts, 4-5 Courts in 1001 Nights Toronto Freehold (plus two smaller Freeholds, seasonal and seelie), Toyko has 3 Moon Princess Courts, and 4 Seasonal Courts in Miami.<br /> <br /> That 17 individual courts to be detailed, including mechanics court contracts, mantle, various merits, bulwark, approaches, court story, court symbols/colours/ranks, court fluff, ect....<br /> <br /> Then each setting has important locations like the CN Tower for example.<br /> <br /> It has a History, plothooks, local weirdness, Huntsmen, and other assorted elements.<br /> <br /> So I think they're bigger word count wise, and that doesn't include more universal Hedge elements in the Hedge section.<br /> <br /> One place I'd love to see done later in another book is Khajuraho in India.</div> </div> </div> </div>The settings chapter is one densely packed monster, I'll tell you that.<br /> <br /> Sooner or later I want to do an Indian setting, but first I want to do the Malay Archipelago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T19:16:01-07:00","id":969606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=969579#post969579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> awesome! have you decided which courts will appear in the Hedge? perhaps Seelie &amp; Unseelie?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have not decided yet. SOON, you'll hear a lot about The Hedge. I'll probably start talking about it in more thorough terms in October or November.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T20:51:07-07:00","id":969637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=969606#post969606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have not decided yet. SOON, you'll hear a lot about The Hedge. I'll probably start talking about it in more thorough terms in October or November.</div> </div> </div> </div>Better question: do you know what settings you want in The Hedge? Getting Dubai in The Pack was an awesome surprise. I totally look forward to seeing some more locales!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T21:38:06-07:00","id":969647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=969637#post969637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Better question: do you know what settings you want in The Hedge? Getting Dubai in The Pack was an awesome surprise. I totally look forward to seeing some more locales!</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure yet. I really have to finish the outline before I can say. I know I want to commit to full-size settings, like the ones you'll see in the core book. So, I can't fit more than like two, and that's pushing it. And I really want cool shit that embodies what the book is about. So, in the Hedge, I need one or two settings that use the way freeholds reshape the Hedge, or similar concepts. <br /> <br /> And FWIW, I might be posting those particular rules in the next day or two. Because I'm polishing the Hedge core rules content right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T00:48:14-07:00","id":969733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=969647#post969647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not sure yet. I really have to finish the outline before I can say. I know I want to commit to full-size settings, like the ones you'll see in the core book. So, I can't fit more than like two, and that's pushing it. And I really want cool shit that embodies what the book is about. So, in the Hedge, I need one or two settings that use the way freeholds reshape the Hedge, or similar concepts.<br /> <br /> And FWIW, I might be posting those particular rules in the next day or two. Because I'm polishing the Hedge core rules content right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the hedge still remains an immensely useful way to travel long distances, a setting like Western Australia+Northern Territories could be useful since then you can have it so the hedge is used to deal with the immense amount of space between settlements. Largest freehold in the world when it comes to land covered, yet one with a normal number of changelings, held together only by it's courts keeping their trods clear and &quot;safe&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T01:01:47-07:00","id":969740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=969647#post969647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not sure yet. I really have to finish the outline before I can say. I know I want to commit to full-size settings, like the ones you'll see in the core book. So, I can't fit more than like two, and that's pushing it. And I really want cool shit that embodies what the book is about. So, in the Hedge, I need one or two settings that use the way freeholds reshape the Hedge, or similar concepts.<br /> <br /> And FWIW, I might be posting those particular rules in the next day or two. Because I'm polishing the Hedge core rules content right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd love to see somewhere where the Hedge breaks from such a literal interpretation; I've wanted a &quot;the sea is the boundary between worlds&quot; Freehold for ages now, and while my American brain really wants that to be Hawaii I could see it being any number of places. A Freehold somewhere in the Arctic Circle might be nice, too, and it also gives a nice excuse to update the (super underloved) Dawn and Dusk Courts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T01:30:32-07:00","id":969751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=969740#post969740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd love to see somewhere where the Hedge breaks from such a literal interpretation; I've wanted a &quot;the sea is the boundary between worlds&quot; Freehold for ages now, and while my American brain really wants that to be Hawaii I could see it being any number of places. A Freehold somewhere in the Arctic Circle might be nice, too, and it also gives a nice excuse to update the (super underloved) Dawn and Dusk Courts.</div> </div> </div> </div>My Hedge is not very literal. <br /> <br /> Of course, the original isn't TECHNICALLY that literal. You'd just never know reading about it beyond the paragraph that says it's not literal. <br /> <br /> Description from the text: <br /> <br /> &quot;Imagine a place built from the insecurities, fears, and wants of everyone nearby. Imagine that as new people enter and leave, the place mutates and warps to amalgamate new ideas with old. Picture strong ideas consuming weaker ideas, picture existential dread consuming disquiet, and all-consuming lust devouring subtle curiosity. Picture all of that, and then make those ideas solid, solid and physically painful.<br /> <br /> In the Hedge, jealousy doesn\u2019t sting, it pricks and snags your skin like an outturned corner of sheet metal, like the one you\u2019d cut yourself on in your dad\u2019s toolshed, the one that made your mom rush you to the hospital over because she was worried you had tetanus. Take a dark alleyway, and line it with thousands of that little metal spike, and toss a few hundred on the ground, and you\u2019re starting to understand the Hedge. Now mix those spikes with all the little nicks and cuts and bruises experienced by everyone that wanders through that alley. The bits that hurt the most jut out the furthest. The ones people will never get over, those block the path so you have to climb over them or duck under them.<br /> <br /> What hurts you will always come back to hurt you and your loved ones again. That\u2019s the Hedge.<br /> <br /> In a direct, literal sense, the Hedge is thought and feeling given shape and life. It\u2019s like one of those little plastic fish that curl and contort based on your body temperature, but it responds to pain and trauma. &quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T01:33:37-07:00","id":969752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=969647#post969647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And FWIW, I might be posting those particular rules in the next day or two. Because I'm polishing the Hedge core rules content right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I look forward to seeing them. I could never figure out how the various rolls given for Hedge navigation actually fit togeather. Hopefully 2E will be better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T01:38:08-07:00","id":969759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=969751#post969751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh believe me, I've known from the 1e corebook onward: the bit about parts of a changeling's soul getting caught on the Thorns as they fled Arcadia was one of the most evocative in the whole line. It's just that some supplements and quite a few unsatisfying chronicles have taken the Hedge as &quot;an endless forest of weird things,&quot; which has been a huge letdown when the Hedge can just as easily be a coral reef and a trackless desert and a surreal psychosphere all at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 09-15-2016, 04:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T02:28:51-07:00","id":969780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=969752#post969752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I look forward to seeing them. I could never figure out how the various rolls given for Hedge navigation actually fit togeather. Hopefully 2E will be better.</div> </div> </div> </div> Me too. It sounds interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T07:47:06-07:00","id":969898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=969759#post969759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh believe me, I've known from the 1e corebook onward: the bit about parts of a changeling's soul getting caught on the Thorns as they fled Arcadia was one of the most evocative in the whole line. It's just that some supplements and quite a few unsatisfying chronicles have taken the Hedge as &quot;an endless forest of weird things,&quot; which has been a huge letdown when the Hedge can just as easily be a coral reef and a trackless desert and a surreal psychosphere all at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's where we got the idea for the Icons, which are now a definitely codified thing that exists. It's palpable. And they're another reason to traverse the Hedge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T08:04:17-07:00","id":969913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/944851-ctl2e-criticisms-from-my-group?p=969759#post969759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh believe me, I've known from the 1e corebook onward: the bit about parts of a changeling's soul getting caught on the Thorns as they fled Arcadia was one of the most evocative in the whole line. It's just that some supplements and quite a few unsatisfying chronicles have taken the Hedge as &quot;an endless forest of weird things,&quot; which has been a huge letdown when the Hedge can just as easily be a coral reef and a trackless desert and a surreal psychosphere all at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hedge as an ocean full of swashbuckling pirate hobs and Changelings needs to happen.<br /> <br /> However the forest of brambles is I think iconic in faerie tales (blame Sleeping Beauty) so I didn't have any problem with it being &quot;the default&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T10:22:00-07:00","id":970017,"title":"","content":"Speaking of the Hedge and Courts, is it possible to have a Freehold in the Hedge? Maybe for some place that has a large area with a sparse population or a nonstandard story where Changelings are rare. So rather than the normal setting be a locale in the world with trips to the Hedge it would be reversed. Just a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}